    "tests": [
      "test/arrowflight.test.js"
    ],
    "equivalent": true,
    "why": "BELT AND BRACES, and recorded as such rather than dressed up as a kill. An orb record never takes the mesh lane's lazy fetch at all (`update`'s `else if (m.gpu === null)`), so `m.gpu` stays null for its whole flight and the draw's own `m.gpu` test already declines it. The `!m.orb` beside it is the SENTENCE - it says which lane this pass is - and it becomes load-bearing the moment anything else ever sets `gpu` on an orb."
  },
